# Roundcube logs as the caddy FPM pool user, so rotation must recreate the files caddy-owned. The
# roundcube-core package rotates the same paths as www-data:adm, which would leave them unwritable and end
# logging silently.
#
# Both this file and the package's cover /var/log/roundcube/*.log, so logrotate reports a duplicate entry
# for whichever it reads second and skips that entire file. Ours is read first because "roundcube" sorts
# before "roundcube-core", which is what makes the correct ownership win - do not rename this file. The
# package's file is a dpkg conffile: deleting it to silence the message would only bring it back on the next
# update, and its ownership would then apply.
#
# The extension-less names come from the package's list. roundcube's log_file_ext defaults to ".log", so
# they are unused today; matching them here means a box configured with an empty log_file_ext still gets
# caddy-owned files instead of falling through to the package's rule.
/var/log/roundcube/*.log
/var/log/roundcube/errors
/var/log/roundcube/sendmail
/var/log/roundcube/session
/var/log/roundcube/userlogins
{
    su caddy caddy
    rotate 12
    monthly
    missingok
    notifempty
    create 0640 caddy caddy
}
